\pard\sa240\qc\b\f0\fs36 Fithub Stakeholder Visual Guide\b0\fs24\par

\pard\sa200\b What This Guide Is\b0\par
\pard\sa160 This guide explains the main Fithub screens in simple language.\par
\pard\sa160 It is written for stakeholders who want to understand:\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - what each screen is for\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - who uses it\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - what action it supports\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - how the app moves from discovery to daily use\par
\pard\sa200 The screenshots for this guide are available in the assets folder beside this file.\par

\pard\sa220\b 1. Home Screen for First-Time Visitors\b0\par
\pard\sa120 Screenshot: assets/01-home-guest.png\par
\pard\sa120\b What this screen is for\b0\par
\pard\sa120 This is the public front door of Fithub.\par
\pard\sa120 It explains the product in a quick, visual way before anyone logs in.\par
\pard\sa120\b Who uses it\b0\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - New visitors\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - Potential members\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - Trainers or gym owners checking what the platform offers\par
\pard\sa120\b What people can do here\b0\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - understand what Fithub does\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - move into login or account creation\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - jump into gym, trainer, or group fitness discovery\par
\pard\sa120\b Simple explanation\b0\par
\pard\sa200 This screen answers the question: "What is Fithub and why should I use it?" It is part marketing page, part entry point into the real app.\par

\pard\sa220\b 2. Discover Screen\b0\par
\pard\sa120 Screenshot: assets/02-discover-overview.png\par
\pard\sa120\b What this screen is for\b0\par
\pard\sa120 This is the browsing area of the platform.\par
\pard\sa120 It helps people explore the kinds of services Fithub supports before they commit to anything.\par
\pard\sa120\b Who uses it\b0\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - Guests\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - Members looking for their next booking\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - Anyone comparing options\par
\pard\sa120\b What people can do here\b0\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - move into gym discovery\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - browse personal training options\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - open group fitness options\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - jump toward meal-plan related experiences\par
\pard\sa120\b Simple explanation\b0\par
\pard\sa200 This is the platform's shopping window. It helps users understand what kinds of fitness options exist inside the system.\par

\pard\sa220\b 3. Login and Account Entry Screen\b0\par
\pard\sa120 Screenshot: assets/03-auth.png\par
\pard\sa120\b What this screen is for\b0\par
\pard\sa120 This screen is the bridge from public browsing into a personal workspace.\par
\pard\sa120 It keeps the app simple by using one shared entry flow for login and account creation.\par
\pard\sa120\b Who uses it\b0\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - Returning users logging in\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - New users creating an account\par
\pard\sa120\b What people can do here\b0\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - sign in\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - create a new account\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - move from guest mode to their role-based dashboard\par
\pard\sa120\b Simple explanation\b0\par
\pard\sa200 This screen says: "Now that you have seen the platform, enter the version of it that belongs to you."\par

\pard\sa220\b 4. Member Home Dashboard\b0\par
\pard\sa120 Screenshot: assets/04-home-member.png\par
\pard\sa120\b What this screen is for\b0\par
\pard\sa120 This is the main day-to-day screen for a member.\par
\pard\sa120 It gathers the basics of personal fitness activity into one place.\par
\pard\sa120\b Who uses it\b0\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - Members\par
\pard\sa120\b What people can do here\b0\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - view their profile summary\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - check session and booking status\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - add body measurements\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - jump to meal plans\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - start a PT or group booking flow\par
\pard\sa120\b Simple explanation\b0\par
\pard\sa200 This is the member's control panel. Instead of making members search across many pages, it puts the most important next actions in one dashboard.\par

\pard\sa220\b 5. Meal Plans Screen\b0\par
\pard\sa120 Screenshot: assets/05-meal-plans.png\par
\pard\sa120\b What this screen is for\b0\par
\pard\sa120 This screen helps a member follow the meal guidance assigned to them.\par
\pard\sa120 It is focused on routine, consistency, and progress tracking.\par
\pard\sa120\b Who uses it\b0\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - Members\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - Trainers indirectly, because their plan structure is reflected here\par
\pard\sa120\b What people can do here\b0\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - see today's meal plan\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - switch between daily, weekly, and monthly views\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - mark meals as completed\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - track adherence over time\par
\pard\sa120\b Simple explanation\b0\par
\pard\sa200 This is the habit-tracking part of Fithub. It turns a meal plan from a static instruction into something a member can actually follow and record.\par

\pard\sa220\b 6. Trainer Workspace\b0\par
\pard\sa120 Screenshot: assets/06-manage-trainer.png\par
\pard\sa120\b What this screen is for\b0\par
\pard\sa120 This is the working area for trainers.\par
\pard\sa120 It is designed to help them operate their coaching business inside the app.\par
\pard\sa120\b Who uses it\b0\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - Trainers\par
\pard\sa120\b What people can do here\b0\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - create or update a trainer profile\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - publish training services\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - review current services\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - manage member requests and bookings\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - work with group program tools\par
\pard\sa120\b Simple explanation\b0\par
\pard\sa200 This is not a marketing page. It is a trainer's operations desk. It gives trainers the tools they need to present offers and manage activity.\par

\pard\sa220\b 7. Gym Owner Workspace\b0\par
\pard\sa120 Screenshot: assets/07-home-owner.png\par
\pard\sa120\b What this screen is for\b0\par
\pard\sa120 This is the operating view for a gym owner or venue operator.\par
\pard\sa120 It combines venue setup, offer publishing, and request handling into one workspace.\par
\pard\sa120\b Who uses it\b0\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - Gym owners\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - Venue operators\par
\pard\sa120\b What people can do here\b0\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - manage the venue profile\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - add products\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - publish passes, memberships, classes, or offers\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - review access requests\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - manage group program related activity\par
\pard\sa120\b Simple explanation\b0\par
\pard\sa200 This is the business side of Fithub. It helps a venue run what it sells and how members access it.\par

\pard\sa220\b 8. Admin Control Center\b0\par
\pard\sa120 Screenshot: assets/08-admin.png\par
\pard\sa120\b What this screen is for\b0\par
\pard\sa120 This is the moderation and oversight area for platform administrators.\par
\pard\sa120 It is where staff monitor the health of the platform and manage sensitive controls.\par
\pard\sa120\b Who uses it\b0\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - Admins\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - Platform operators\par
\pard\sa120\b What people can do here\b0\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - review user accounts\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - activate or deactivate users\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - moderate trainers\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - inspect bookings\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - oversee shops and platform totals\par
\pard\sa120\b Simple explanation\b0\par
\pard\sa200 This is the governance layer of Fithub. It exists so the platform can be supervised without mixing admin controls into the normal member or trainer experience.\par

\pard\sa220\b How the Full Product Flow Works\b0\par
\pard\sa120 In simple terms, Fithub moves people through four stages:\par
\pard\li360\sa120 1. Discover what is available.\par
\pard\li360\sa120 2. Sign in or create an account.\par
\pard\li360\sa120 3. Enter a dashboard that matches the user's role.\par
\pard\li360\sa120 4. Use that dashboard to manage bookings, plans, offers, or oversight.\par
\pard\sa120 That means Fithub is not only a fitness listing site.\par
\pard\sa120 It is a role-based platform where different people use the same product for different jobs:\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - members manage their fitness activity\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - trainers manage coaching services\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - gym owners manage venue offers\par
\pard\li360\sa120 - admins monitor the platform\par

\pard\sa220\b Quick Stakeholder Summary\b0\par
\pard\sa120 If you want the shortest explanation possible, it is this:\par
\pard\sa120 Fithub starts as a discovery platform, then becomes a role-based fitness workspace after login. Members get a personal dashboard, trainers get service management tools, gym owners get venue management tools, and admins get oversight controls.\par
}
